{
 "description": "E2E (mod): approvals (command allow / for the session / decline with a reason, file change), a permissions grant, requestUserInput questions, a plan and a todo list, a subagent, slow thinking (top level, a subagent's and a nested subagent's), a steer, an interrupt.",
 "model": "gpt-5.6-luna",
 "effort": "low",
 "approvalPolicy": "untrusted",
 "sandbox": "workspace-write",
 "approvalsReviewer": "user",
 "prompts": [
  {
   "match": "run the tests",
   "once": false,
   "steps": [
    {
     "text": "Running the tests.",
     "phase": "commentary"
    },
    {
     "command": "npm test",
     "output": [
      "\u001b[32m✓\u001b[39m parses numbers\n",
      "\u001b[32m✓\u001b[39m trims input\n"
     ],
     "approval": {
      "availableDecisions": [
       "accept",
       "acceptForSession",
       "decline",
       "cancel"
      ],
      "reason": "Runs the test suite"
     }
    },
    {
     "text": "All tests pass."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "match": "clean",
   "once": false,
   "steps": [
    {
     "command": "rm -rf build",
     "approval": {
      "availableDecisions": [
       "accept",
       "acceptForSession",
       "decline",
       "cancel"
      ],
      "reason": "Deletes the build folder"
     },
     "onDecline": [
      {
       "text": "Left the build folder alone."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "Cleaned."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "match": "edit",
   "once": false,
   "steps": [
    {
     "fileChange": [
      {
       "path": "src/a.ts",
       "kind": "update",
       "diff": "@@ -1 +1 @@\n-export const a = 1;\n+export const a = 2;\n"
      }
     ],
     "approval": {
      "reason": "Bump a"
     }
    },
    {
     "text": "Edited src/a.ts."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "match": "network",
   "once": false,
   "steps": [
    {
     "permissions": {
      "reason": "Needs the network to fetch the schema",
      "permissions": {
       "network": {
        "enabled": true
       },
       "fileSystem": null
      }
     },
     "then": {
      "session": [
       {
        "text": "Network granted for the session."
       }
      ],
      "turn": [
       {
        "text": "Network granted for this turn."
       }
      ],
      "*": [
       {
        "text": "No network, then."
       }
      ]
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "match": "ask me",
   "once": false,
   "steps": [
    {
     "question": {
      "questions": [
       {
        "id": "db",
        "header": "Database",
        "question": "Which database should the service use?",
        "isOther": true,
        "isSecret": false,
        "options": [
         {
          "label": "Postgres",
          "description": "What the other services use"
         },
         {
          "label": "SQLite",
          "description": "One file, no server"
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "id": "name",
        "header": "Name",
        "question": "What should the service be called?",
        "isOther": false,
        "isSecret": false,
        "options": null
       }
      ]
     },
     "then": {
      "*": [
       {
        "text": "Using {answer}."
       }
      ]
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "match": "check the server",
   "once": false,
   "steps": [
    {
     "elicitation": {
      "serverName": "figma",
      "mode": "form",
      "_meta": null,
      "message": "Go on?",
      "requestedSchema": {
       "type": "object",
       "properties": {}
      }
     },
     "then": {
      "accept": [
       {
        "text": "Figma went on."
       }
      ],
      "*": [
       {
        "text": "Figma stopped."
       }
      ]
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "match": "make a plan",
   "once": false,
   "steps": [
    {
     "todo": {
      "explanation": "Fix the parser and prove it.",
      "plan": [
       {
        "step": "Read the parser",
        "status": "completed"
       },
       {
        "step": "Fix the trimming",
        "status": "inProgress"
       },
       {
        "step": "Run the tests",
        "status": "pending"
       }
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "plan": "# Plan\n\n1. Read the parser\n2. Fix the trimming\n3. Run the tests"
    },
    {
     "text": "That's the plan."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "match": "agent",
   "once": false,
   "steps": [
    {
     "subagent": {
      "prompt": "Find the flaky test.",
      "steps": [
       {
        "reasoning": [
         "**Looking**"
        ]
       },
       {
        "command": "rg flaky tests",
        "output": "tests/a.test.ts:12\n"
       },
       {
        "text": "tests/a.test.ts sleeps."
       }
      ],
      "answer": "tests/a.test.ts: a fixed sleep."
     }
    },
    {
     "text": "The subagent found it: tests/a.test.ts sleeps."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "match": "think it over",
   "note": "Each reasoning streams 4 chars every 100 ms on purpose: the top-level one for ~7 s, the subagent's for ~16 s, the nested one's for ~10 s. flows-v3's 'thinking shows once' step folds and opens cards while they stream, so shorter text fails it.",
   "once": false,
   "steps": [
    {
     "reasoning": [
      "Weighing the options before I answer: the cache, the queue, the retry. Weighing the options before I answer: the cache, the queue, the retry. Weighing the options before I answer: the cache, the queue, the retry. Weighing the options before I answer: the cache, the queue, the retry."
     ],
     "chunk": 4,
     "every": 100
    },
    {
     "subagent": {
      "prompt": "Check the call sites.",
      "steps": [
       {
        "reasoning": [
         "Reading the call sites one by one to see who retries and who gives up. Reading the call sites one by one to see who retries and who gives up. Reading the call sites one by one to see who retries and who gives up. Reading the call sites one by one to see who retries and who gives up. Reading the call sites one by one to see who retries and who gives up. Reading the call sites one by one to see who retries and who gives up. Reading the call sites one by one to see who retries and who gives up. Reading the call sites one by one to see who retries and who gives up. Reading the call sites one by one to see who retries and who gives up."
        ],
        "chunk": 4,
        "every": 100
       },
       {
        "subagent": {
         "prompt": "Read the retry helper.",
         "steps": [
          {
           "reasoning": [
            "The helper backs off twice, then gives up and reports the error. The helper backs off twice, then gives up and reports the error. The helper backs off twice, then gives up and reports the error. The helper backs off twice, then gives up and reports the error. The helper backs off twice, then gives up and reports the error. The helper backs off twice, then gives up and reports the error."
           ],
           "chunk": 4,
           "every": 100
          },
          {
           "text": "It backs off twice."
          }
         ],
         "answer": "It backs off twice."
        }
       },
       {
        "text": "Two call sites retry."
       }
      ],
      "answer": "Two call sites retry."
     }
    },
    {
     "text": "Thought it over: retry in one place."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "match": "long job",
   "once": false,
   "steps": [
    {
     "text": "Starting the long job.",
     "phase": "commentary"
    },
    {
     "command": "make build",
     "output": [
      "compiling\n",
      "linking\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "waitFor": "steer",
     "timeout": 8000
    },
    {
     "text": "Done with the long job."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "match": "also check the logs",
   "once": false,
   "steps": [
    {
     "text": "Checked the logs too."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "match": "stall",
   "once": false,
   "steps": [
    {
     "command": "sleep 100",
     "output": "",
     "until": "interrupt",
     "tick": "waiting {n}\n",
     "every": 300
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "match": "wrap up the todos",
   "once": false,
   "steps": [
    {
     "todo": {
      "plan": [
       {
        "step": "Read the parser",
        "status": "completed"
       },
       {
        "step": "Fix the trimming",
        "status": "completed"
       },
       {
        "step": "Run the tests",
        "status": "completed"
       }
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "text": "Every step is done."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "match": "start a new list",
   "once": false,
   "steps": [
    {
     "todo": {
      "plan": [
       {
        "step": "Write the notes",
        "status": "pending"
       }
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "text": "A new list."
    }
   ]
  }
 ],
 "default": [
  {
   "text": "ok: {prompt}"
  }
 ]
}
